WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.920
Beards, braids, and blood – transforming&nbsp;
into a viking isn't easy. Except for one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:11.280
actress who was pretty much born for the part.&nbsp;
Find out who, and so much more right here!

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:17.120
Australian actor Sam Corlett portrays&nbsp;
the legendary explorer Leif Erikson,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:22.080
the Norseman who is thought to have been the&nbsp;
first European to have set foot in North America,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:27.040
centuries before Christopher Columbus. In&nbsp;
a promotional packet provided to the press,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:30.720
Netflix describes the Erikson of&nbsp;
"Vikings: Valhalla," saying, 
 &nbsp;

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:34.800
"[He’s] a Greenlander raised on the outer&nbsp;
fringes of the known world, [who] comes from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:40.000
a tightly-knit family steeped in pagan beliefs." 
 
It goes on to say that although Leif is an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:45.520
intrepid sailor and physically tough, he is&nbsp;
also thoughtful and often quiet, and apparently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:50.640
relatively new to the Viking world — which is&nbsp;
in the, quote, “throes of violent change.”
 &nbsp;

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:55.280
When Corlett was a teenager, he actually&nbsp;
watched the original "Vikings" with his father,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:59.920
so it's fitting that he would go on to star in its&nbsp;
spinoff. The real-life Corlett still has the long&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:05.200
hair and facial hair of his Viking counterpart,&nbsp;
but keeps it much more neatly trimmed and styled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:10.960
than Erikson. On set, Corlett -- who is vegan --&nbsp;
was costumed in vegan leather armor to honor his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:15.920
personal convictions. This is another distinct&nbsp;
difference between the actor and the character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:17.880
he'll be portraying.
 
[Yelling]
 

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:24.400
One of the most beloved characters on&nbsp;
"Vikings" was the shieldmaiden Lagertha,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:30.240
played by Katheryn Winnick. So viewers are likely&nbsp;
eager to see another female Viking warrior rise up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:35.680
in the "Valhalla" character Freydis Eriksdotter.&nbsp;
Netflix's description for Frida reads, 
 &nbsp;

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:39.680
"Fiery and headstrong, Freydis is&nbsp;
a staunch believer in the old gods&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:45.040
and a fierce pagan. Like her brother Leif, she&nbsp;
reaches Kattegat as an outsider but becomes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:49.600
an inspiration to those of the old ways."
 
Freydis will be portrayed by Swedish model&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:54.080
Frida Gustavsson, who has had an impressive&nbsp;
career walking in shows for some of the world's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:59.680
most celebrated designers. As one might expect of&nbsp;
someone with Gustavsson's professional background,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:04.480
her real-life look is much more polished than&nbsp;
the armored and intricately braided Freydis.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:08.880
In what feels like a cosmic coincidence,&nbsp;
Gustavsson's real-life nickname is also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:13.200
"Freydis," and her actual father and&nbsp;
brother are also named Erik and Leif,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:15.840
just like those of her character in the show.
 

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:22.320
"Vikings" viewers will remember King Harald,&nbsp;
played by Peter Franzén, who appeared in seasons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:26.880
four through six of the series as a leader&nbsp;
determined to be crowned king of all Norway.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:30.880
"Vikings: Valhalla" will follow one&nbsp;
of his descendants, Harald Sigurdsson,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:35.440
who carries the same ambition as his&nbsp;
ancestor. His Netflix bio reads, 
 &nbsp;

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:40.720
"Born into Viking nobility, Harald is one of the&nbsp;
last Viking berserkers and a Prince of Norway&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:46.800
intent on becoming King of Norway. Charismatic,&nbsp;
ambitious, and handsome, he is able to unite both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:49.840
Christian and pagan Vikings."
 
“Keep an eye on him.”
 &nbsp;

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:55.440
Harald will be portrayed by English actor&nbsp;
Leo Suter, who bears very little resemblance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.440 --> 00:03:00.800
to his Viking character. While Harald sports the&nbsp;
typical Viking look of a full beard and long hair,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:05.520
Suter typically tends to prefer going clean-shaven&nbsp;
and keeping his hair cropped fairly short.
 

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:10.000
Some actors need to undergo greater&nbsp;
transformations than others for their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:14.960
roles in "Vikings: Valhalla," and actor Bradley&nbsp;
Freegard may be one of the least altered for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:20.800
his role as King Canute, the King of Denmark. The&nbsp;
Netflix press materials describe Canute, saying, 
 &nbsp;

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:25.760
"A wise, savvy, and ruthless Viking leader.&nbsp;
He keeps his friends close and his enemies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:30.320
closer. Canute's ambitions will mold the&nbsp;
course of history in the 11th century and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:35.440
make him a defining figure of the Viking Age."
 
In real life, Welsh actor Freegard doesn't look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:40.800
too remarkably different from his character. Both&nbsp;
have dark hair and full beards, although Canute&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:46.160
keeps his black hair long and tightly pulled back,&nbsp;
while Freegard wears his cut short and allows some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:51.200
of the natural gray to peek through. Freegard also&nbsp;
keeps his beard trimmed to a much shorter length&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:56.640
than Canute's. Canute's family play a central role&nbsp;
in "Vikings: Valhalla," with his wife and father&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.640 --> 00:04:02.320
also vying for power as Canute works to make sure&nbsp;
Denmark remains on top of the political hierarchy.

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:07.520
It wouldn't be a "Vikings" story without&nbsp;
feuding siblings, and "Valhalla" promises&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:13.600
that in spades. Icelandic actor Jóhannes&nbsp;
Haukur Jóhannesson portrays Olaf Haraldsson,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:18.400
Sigurdsson's older half-brother and Prince&nbsp;
of Norway. Olaf is first in line for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:23.040
Norwegian throne, which we imagine will be a&nbsp;
point of contention between him and Harald.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:26.640
Olaf's Netflix bio reads, 
 
"Ambitious, unforgiving,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:31.680
and a physical force to be reckoned with, Olaf&nbsp;
is also an extremely devout Christian Viking." 
 &nbsp;

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:36.400
"Vikings" viewers will remember that the former&nbsp;
priest Athelstan was the first practicing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:40.640
Christian to live among the Vikings, although&nbsp;
the conflict between his beliefs and those of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:44.880
his Viking neighbors ultimately led to his&nbsp;
death. It will be interesting to see how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:50.400
those dynamics have shifted over a century later.
 
In real life, Jóhannesson has kept the long, full&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:55.440
beard of his character, but not his long hair,&nbsp;
preferring instead a style that is cut close on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.440 --> 00:05:00.800
the sides and slightly longer on top. In addition&nbsp;
to being one of the main cast members of "Vikings:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:06.560
Valhalla," Jóhannes Haukur Jóhannesson is also an&nbsp;
accomplished chef. The Netflix press kit mentions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:11.440
that he was frequently known to bring in homemade&nbsp;
baked goods for the stunt crew during rehearsals.
 

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:16.160
Of the Viking leader Jarl Haakon,&nbsp;
Netflix's press packet reads, 
 &nbsp;

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:20.880
"A great warrior and tolerant leader,&nbsp;
Haakon rules Kattegat with a steady hand.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:25.920
Though pagan, she has managed to keep Kattegat&nbsp;
a city open to all faiths in a challenging time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:30.160
She will become a powerful mentor to&nbsp;
Freydis, who is drawn to her wisdom." 
 &nbsp;

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:33.840
Of course, we know from watching Ragnar's&nbsp;
struggles in "Vikings" just how difficult&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:38.800
it can be to maintain peace between people of&nbsp;
different faiths in Kattegat. So it will be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:44.240
interesting to see how Jarl Haakon manages to pull&nbsp;
that off -- if such a thing is even possible.
 &nbsp;

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:49.840
“I want to be reunited with my Christian friend.”
 
Jarl Haakon will be played by Danish-Swedish&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:55.200
singer Caroline Henderson, who is known primarily&nbsp;
for her more recent jazz albums after previously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.200 --> 00:06:00.560
singing mostly pop. Jarl Haakon is one of very few&nbsp;
Viking women we've seen in promotional materials&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:05.120
who seems to wear her hair loose more often&nbsp;
than not. So, her normal appearance is not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:08.960
quite as drastic of a shift from her&nbsp;
Viking look as some of her castmates.
 

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:14.640
"Valhalla" will feature the family of one&nbsp;
of Alfred, King of Wessex’s descendants:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:17.600
King Aethelred II, and Aethelred's wife,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:21.760
Emma of Normandy. This is what the&nbsp;
Netflix press packet has to say of Emma: 
 &nbsp;

00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:26.880
"The young, ambitious Emma of Normandy is from&nbsp;
the Norman court in France, and of Viking blood.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:32.080
She is now married to King Aethelred II, the&nbsp;
current King of England. Politically astute&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:36.640
and one of the wealthiest women in Europe,&nbsp;
Queen Emma is a sharp and capable leader."
 &nbsp;

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:40.880
Emma seems to follow in a long tradition of&nbsp;
shrewd queens on "Vikings," and is portrayed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:45.920
by German actor and model Laura Berlin. On&nbsp;
"Valhalla," Emma's hair is a dark brown,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:51.200
but in real life, Berlin's hair color has run&nbsp;
the full spectrum of colors, from dark to light,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:56.160
and even a vibrant purple at one point. Berlin&nbsp;
has worked as a model since she was a teenager,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:59.920
making her no stranger to the intricate&nbsp;
costumes she needs to wear as Emma. 
 

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:04.480
Described in Netflix's press&nbsp;
materials for "Vikings: Valhalla" as,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:08.720
quote, "the ultimate survivor," David&nbsp;
Oakes' character, the Earl of Godwin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:12.480
serves as chief counselor to the&nbsp;
King of England, Aethelred II.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:17.200
Of Godwin's character, the description reads: 
 
"Godwin was born on the political fringes and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:22.800
is haunted by his late father's mistakes. Cunning&nbsp;
and savvy, he knows how to make powerful allies."
 &nbsp;

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:28.160
Godwin's portrayer is English actor David&nbsp;
Oakes, who is no stranger to historical dramas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:32.640
thanks to his work on shows such as "The&nbsp;
Borgias," "The White Queen," and "Victoria." 
 

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:37.680
"Vikings" introduced us to the complicated&nbsp;
world of English royal succession,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:42.560
and "Vikings: Valhalla" continues that theme&nbsp;
with Prince Edmund, played by English actor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:48.480
Louis Davison. His official Netflix bio reads,
 
"King Aethelred II's son with his first deceased&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:53.840
wife and now Emma of Normandy's stepson, Edmund&nbsp;
is first in line to inherit the English throne.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:58.320
Edmund is nervous to lead, but will play a&nbsp;
vital role in deciding England's future."
 &nbsp;

00:07:58.880 --> 00:08:02.080
Davison is still a relative&nbsp;
newcomer to the world of television,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:06.240
only appearing in a few roles before&nbsp;
landing his part on "Vikings: Valhalla."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:10.640
In real life, Davison's hair is much lighter&nbsp;
than Edmund's dark color, and although it is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:14.720
still not long, he tends to wear it much&nbsp;
more loosely than Edmund's severe style.
 

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:21.360
Season 4 of "Vikings" introduced us to Aethelred,&nbsp;
the legitimate son of King Aethelwulf and his wife&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:25.440
Judith. Unfortunately for Aethelred,&nbsp;
Judith liked her younger son more,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:30.560
and poisoned Aethelred rather than allowing him&nbsp;
to assume the throne. "Vikings: Valhalla" picks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:35.360
up a few generations down this dysfunctional&nbsp;
family lineage, with Alfred's descendant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:40.240
Aethelred II now on the English throne. 
 
Portraying Aethelred II on "Vikings:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:45.760
Valhalla" is veteran Irish actor Bosco Hogan.&nbsp;
He previously appeared in Season 5 of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:51.200
original "Vikings" series as the Lord Abbot at the&nbsp;
Lindisfarne monastery in the episode "Full Moon."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:55.360
Hogan's look for "Valhalla" won't be tremendously&nbsp;
different from his real-life appearance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.360 --> 00:08:59.600
with the addition only of a trim gray&nbsp;
beard — and, of course, a royal wardrobe.
 

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:03.520
It wouldn't be a "Vikings" show&nbsp;
without some religious extremism,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:08.160
and in "Valhalla," it seems that box will&nbsp;
be checked by Jarl Kåre, played by Danish&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:14.480
actor Asbjørn Nissen. His Netflix bio reads, 
 
"A mysterious and chilling figure, Jarl Kåre&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.480 --> 00:09:19.040
is a murderous Christian zealot who presents&nbsp;
a very real threat to the old pagan ways." 
 &nbsp;

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:24.400
This sounds almost as though Jarl Kåre will act&nbsp;
as a kind of reverse spiritual successor to Floki,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.400 --> 00:09:28.880
played by Gustaf Skarsgård. After all,&nbsp;
he was the devout "Vikings" character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:32.560
whose spiritual convictions led him&nbsp;
to eventually murder Athelstan.
 &nbsp;

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:36.080
In real life, Nissen still has the&nbsp;
bald head and long, thick beard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:38.800
that Jarl Kåre sports in "Valhalla," although it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:42.240
looks like he takes much better care of&nbsp;
his beard than his Viking counterpart.
 

00:09:43.280 --> 00:09:48.720
Concerning Queen Aelfgifu, played by Pollyanna&nbsp;
McIntosh, Netflix's press packet reads, 
 &nbsp;

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:54.080
"She uses her charm and guile to great effect as&nbsp;
she promotes the interests of her Mercian homeland&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:58.400
and tries to assert herself in her husband&nbsp;
King Canute's growing power structure." 
 &nbsp;

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:03.120
The Scottish actress takes on the role of the&nbsp;
formidable Queen Aelfgifu with a look on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:08.240
show seeing her donning elaborate blonde tresses.&nbsp;
This is a big step away from McIntosh's look in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:13.360
real life. Although the actor has indeed been&nbsp;
blonde before, she is currently a brunette and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:18.560
has recently been keeping her hair cut extremely&nbsp;
short for her role as Jadis in "The Walking Dead"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.560 --> 00:10:21.920
and "The Walking Dead: World Beyond."
 
“You’ll be answering to me.”
 

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:26.400
The final member of the main "Vikings:&nbsp;
Valhalla" cast is Danish actor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:32.400
Søren Pilmark. He plays King Sweyn Forkbeard, who&nbsp;
Netflix describes in their press materials as, 
 &nbsp;

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:35.920
"King Canute's father, who is&nbsp;
far less diplomatic than his son.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:39.520
He will do whatever it takes to&nbsp;
protect his family's place of power,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.520 --> 00:10:43.520
and has no tolerance for traitors or&nbsp;
those who question his authority." 
 &nbsp;

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:48.320
Of course, when it comes to "Vikings," we have&nbsp;
a feeling that "less diplomatic" tends to mean&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.320 --> 00:10:52.880
"ruthless and violent." So it will be interesting&nbsp;
to see how far the Danish king is willing to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:57.600
go in his quest to hold onto his power.
 
In "Vikings: Valhalla," Pilmark is nearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.600 --> 00:11:02.480
unrecognizable as King Sweyn Forkbeard,&nbsp;
whose graying hair is long and wild,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.480 --> 00:11:07.840
looking as though he's forgotten to comb it since,&nbsp;
well, ever. Contrasted to Pilmark's real-life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.840 --> 00:11:12.240
appearance, in which the actor is typically&nbsp;
clean-shaven and short-haired, Pilmark's role&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.240 --> 00:11:16.720
may be one of the most dramatic transformations&nbsp;
among the cast of "Vikings: Valhalla.”

